&lt;p&gt;      05&sol;2006 - Pancreas transplants alone are covered under Medicare in limited circumstances. Effective date 04&sol;26&sol;2006. Implementation date for Carriers no later than 07&sol;03&sol;2006. Effective date for FI&#39;s 10&sol;02&sol;2006. (&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;Regulations-and-Guidance&sol;Guidance&sol;Transmittals&sol;Downloads&sol;R56ncd.pdf&quot;&gt;TN 56&lt;&sol;a&gt;) (CR 5093)&lt;&sol;p&gt;    

&lt;p&gt;      07&sol;2004 - Covered costs of transplantation of pancreatic islet cell, but only in context of an NIH-sponsored clinical trial. Effective date 10&sol;01&sol;2004. Implementation date 10&sol;04&sol;2004. (&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;Regulations-and-Guidance&sol;Guidance&sol;Transmittals&sol;Downloads&sol;R18ncd.pdf&quot;&gt;TN 18&lt;&sol;a&gt;) (CR 3385)&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;      04&sol;2000 - Corrected ICD-9-CM code from 52.83 to 52.82, and deleted reference to 36-month period of entitlement. Effective and implementation dates 10&sol;01&sol;2000. (&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;Regulations-and-Guidance&sol;Guidance&sol;Transmittals&sol;Downloads&sol;R124CIM.pdf&quot;&gt;TN 124&lt;&sol;a&gt;) (CR 1132)&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;      08&sol;1999 - Removed requirement that procedure must be performed simultaneously with or after a Medicare covered kidney transplant. Effective and implementation dates 07&sol;01&sol;1999. (TN 119) (CR 929)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;      04&sol;1999 - Specified that procedure only covered when performed simultaneously with or after a Medicare covered kidney transplant. Noncoverage of procedure continues for patients who have not experienced end stage renal failure secondary to diabetes. Effective date 07&sol;01&sol;1999. (TN 115) (CR 818)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
